1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:29,529
<i>Arnaldo, Arnaldo.</i>

6
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:32,073
<i>Arnaldo, you're not crazy. Do you hear me?</i>

7
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:35,577
<i>I won't let you throw away</i>
<i>everything I've done for you.</i>

8
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:38,371
[maid] Ma'am Emilia!

9
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,166
-[Emilia screams]
<i>-Arnaldo!</i>

10
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,459
[gunshot]

11
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:44,502
[Julio] <i>Ivy, Arnaldo…</i>

12
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:48,465
<i>Arnaldo is in the hospital.</i>
<i>He's fighting for his life.</i>

13
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:53,887
[Ivy] <i>You don't deserve to die,</i>
<i>Arnaldo. You need to live.</i>

14
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:57,807
<i>I'm not through with the Ardientes.</i>

15
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:00,727
<i>You have to accept the fact</i>
<i>that Arnaldo is not well!</i>

16
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:03,730
[Julio] <i>No one tells</i>
<i>Julio Ardiente what to do!</i>

17
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,106
[Ivy] <i>I have decided.</i>

18
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>I will go back to Arnaldo</i>
<i>and take care of him.</i>

19
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:11,821
[Julio] <i>Without Ivy, Arnaldo will die.</i>

20
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>You will accept the fact that</i>
<i>Miss Aguas is here to stay.</i>

21
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,619
[Camia] <i>Now that you're</i>
<i>going after Emilia,</i>

22
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:21,247
<i>it's my right as your mother</i>
<i>to know about all your plans.</i>

23
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:24,292
<i>I'll strip her of her wealth</i>
<i>and family name.</i>

24
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:28,671
<i>I'm sure that the Ardientes will do</i>
<i>everything for Arnaldo to get well,</i>

25
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,799
<i>but I won't make it easy for them.</i>

26
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,802
<i>I won't let Arnaldo</i>
<i>get back on his feet again.</i>

27
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:36,054
[Natalie] <i>I know you want</i>
<i>something from me.</i>

28
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:39,015
<i>I saw that Arnaldo is getting sick.</i>

29
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:39,974
<i>Let's not kid ourselves.</i>

30
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:42,393
[Raul] <i>Fine. Eight o'clock.</i>
<i>The usual place.</i>

31
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,981
A public announcement.

32
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:50,860
We just need to make
a public announcement as well.

33
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:53,822
A press conference, Congressman.
That's what we'll do.

34
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:56,407
What? A press conference?

35
00:01:56,491 --> 00:02:01,621
Do you want people to talk about
Arnaldo's suicide attempt?

36
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:03,706
You're out of your mind! Where's Raul?

37
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:07,210
You shouldn't be looking
for someone who's not here

38
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:11,047
because I'm sure he's busy
with someone else.

39
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:12,298
We don't need him.

40
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,717
Raul is Arnaldo's father.

41
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:17,720
Obviously, his opinion matters
more than yours.

42
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:20,557
Let Ivy speak.

43
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,104
Thank you, Congressman.

44
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:36,906
My plan is to not announce
what really happened to Arnaldo.

45
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,535
The key is taking control
of the situation.

46
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:45,165
We'll just tell them
what needs to be said.

47
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:49,586
-Miss Aguas is right.
-Hmm?

48
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:53,214
What's important is for us to mold

49
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:56,593
the people's opinion of Arnaldo.

50
00:02:58,511 --> 00:03:02,891
Schedule a press conference.
I have an announcement to make.

51
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:05,101
[tense music playing]

52
00:03:21,075 --> 00:03:24,579
Anna. Are you okay?

53
00:03:26,831 --> 00:03:28,374
You seemed angry earlier.

54
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:36,507
Do you know how painful it is
to find out Arnaldo's case

55
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:38,384
was dismissed and he's free now?

56
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:42,555
Diego, he killed my foster mother…

57
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:47,518
along with my dreams
we all had for ourselves.

58
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:53,066
He also killed my friend. And many others.

59
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:59,614
You know, Anna, even as kids,

60
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:03,284
Arnaldo treated me like dirt,
like we weren't brothers.

61
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:06,996
It's easy to get angry and retaliate,

62
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,791
but we have to watch our actions.

63
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:13,836
We'll attain justice the right way.

64
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:17,632
One day, he'll pay for his crimes.

65
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:25,890
Congressman, according
to the camp of Diego Torillo,

66
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:26,933
Camia, and Lily Cruz,

67
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:28,768
they won't stop until
Mayor Arnaldo is behind bars.

68
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:30,019
What can you say about this?

69
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:33,273
To my beloved children,

70
00:04:34,065 --> 00:04:36,359
the citizens of Poblacion Ardiente,

71
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:41,823
<i>this is the first time</i>
<i>I'll face you like this.</i>

72
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:47,453
<i>With a heavy and broken heart.</i>

73
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:54,919
<i>Because your beloved mayor is gravely ill.</i>

74
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:59,007
[reporter] <i>Care to be specific,</i>
<i>Congressman?</i>

75
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:03,594
[Julio] <i>I don't want to go</i>
<i>into the specifics.</i>

76
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:06,222
<i>All I can tell you is,</i>

77
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:11,769
<i>Arnaldo will be on</i>
<i>an indefinite sick leave.</i>

78
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:14,647
<i>And in the meantime,</i>

79
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:18,276
I kindly ask everyone to pray
for his speedy recovery.

80
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:20,320
So, who will be the acting mayor?

81
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:22,530
And what about his candidacy?

82
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:25,867
[Julio] <i>We will follow the rule of law.</i>

83
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:30,538
<i>The vice mayor shall be the acting mayor.</i>

84
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:34,542
<i>As soon as Arnaldo is discharged</i>
<i>from the hospital,</i>

85
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:37,795
<i>he will continue</i>
<i>campaigning</i>

86
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,005
<i>for his candidacy</i>

87
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:41,174
<i>as our next governor.</i>

88
00:05:44,093 --> 00:05:46,429
<i>Again, to all the citizens</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente,</i>

89
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:50,892
<i>who I regard as my children,</i>

90
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:56,147
<i>our family is once again going</i>
<i>through another rough patch.</i>

91
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:58,399
<i>But despite this,</i>

92
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:07,950
<i>we thank all of you for your</i>
<i>never-ending support for us.</i>

93
00:06:09,994 --> 00:06:12,705
<i>Let's all keep praying</i>
<i>for our mayor.</i>

94
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,876
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

95
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:20,671
His interview is trending on social media.

96
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:25,635
According to one user, "I feel
sorry for Congressman Ardiente.

97
00:06:25,718 --> 00:06:28,304
Clearly, he loves his grandson."

98
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:30,807
-Let me see.
-Look at all these posts!

99
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:32,433
Here's another one.

100
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:37,563
"I hope Mayor Arnaldo gets well soon so
our beloved congressman will cheer up."

101
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,523
[Pandoy exclaims]

102
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:41,609
Obviously, they're looking for sympathy.

103
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:42,819
-[Marlon] Typical.
-Here's another one.

104
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:46,948
"Poor mayor, he's sick.
I'll vote for him as governor."

105
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:49,700
-[man] Geez!
-[Marlon] They all pity him.

106
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:50,993
[man 2] Looks like it.

107
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:52,120
This is bad.

108
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:54,956
We need to get these people
to sympathize with us.

109
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:57,583
We'll re-file the charges as planned.

110
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,961
And we'll continue our campaign.

111
00:07:00,628 --> 00:07:04,632
Let's remind the public that
this happened to their mayor

112
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:08,136
not because he should be pitied,
but because he deserved it.

113
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:12,014
He must be imprisoned for all his crimes!

114
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,893
[tense music playing]

115
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:32,368
Jepoy, the Ardientes
are playing with the situation.

116
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:35,329
Even though Arnaldo's crimes
were made public,

117
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:37,665
they can get the sympathy of the people.

118
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:41,878
To think they feel sorry for
a family of soulless murderers

119
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:44,130
and expressed support for Arnaldo!

120
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:48,009
Jepoy, I'm worried
that Arnaldo might get away

121
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:50,303
with what he did to Aunt Carlotta!

122
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:55,016
[door closing]

123
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:07,987
[reporter] <i>In other news,</i>
<i>a woman hanged herself</i>

124
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,614
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

125
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:12,909
<i>She was later identified</i>
<i>as Carlotta Navarro,</i>

126
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:16,204
<i>caretaker of businesswoman, Ivy Aguas.</i>

127
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:19,332
<i>This has been Dennis Pangilinan,</i>
<i>reporting for ATV.</i>

128
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:21,125
[cries]

129
00:08:21,792 --> 00:08:24,837
<i>Auntie!</i>

130
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:31,969
<i>Auntie Carlotta!</i>

131
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:33,763
<i>Anna?</i>

132
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:40,520
[Anna] <i>Jepoy, Auntie is dead!</i>

133
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:42,230
[grunts]

134
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:47,485
<i>Jepoy, Auntie is dead! Jepoy…</i>

135
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:54,700
[Anna] Jepoy, we made a promise
that day, remember?

136
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:57,119
We swore to help each other.

137
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:00,456
Help me take revenge on Arnaldo.

138
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:07,713
Anna, that was not part of our agreement.

139
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,507
That's not part of our plans.

140
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,634
But, Jepoy, everything we're
fighting for will be for nothing

141
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:13,219
if Arnaldo stays in power.

142
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:15,513
I can't let him become the next governor!

143
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:16,681
Fine.

144
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:20,017
So, what's your plan?

145
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:23,604
Thank you, miss. We'll go now.

146
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:25,147
Thank you so much, sir.

147
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,401
[suspenseful music playing]

148
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,034
Yes, ma'am?

149
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,829
-Room 272?
-Okay, ma'am.

150
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:44,709
Here, ma'am. Thank you so much.

151
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:45,876
Thank you.

152
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,317
[Emilia] This is all Ivy's fault.

153
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,402
She's behind this press conference.

154
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:14,238
And how can you not have
a statement, Papa?

155
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:17,992
Vice Mayor Romero? Are you kidding me?

156
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:23,581
He is the rightful acting mayor,

157
00:10:23,664 --> 00:10:27,001
as far as the law of the land
is concerned,

158
00:10:27,084 --> 00:10:31,047
while Arnaldo is still in the hospital.

159
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:32,590
And one more thing.

160
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:36,594
Nobody's going to replace
Arnaldo in the election.

161
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:39,805
When Arnaldo wins the governorship,

162
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:42,224
I should be the mayor of this town, Papa.

163
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:44,769
Especially now that I have
an annulment case ongoing,

164
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:47,063
I have all the time for public service.

165
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:48,147
Hmm…

166
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:53,819
You may have the time,
but you left out one thing.

167
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:59,200
Intelligence. That position needs a brain.

168
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:03,120
I used to be the governor
and mayor of this town, Papa.

169
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:06,415
Stress on the words "used to."

170
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:10,878
Don't be so surprised
that you've been demoted.

171
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:16,384
Don't even be proud of your term
of office because, to be honest,

172
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:18,636
you didn't accomplish anything

173
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:21,514
except for being an embarrassment

174
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:24,934
and a landfill of dead bodies

175
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:27,186
of the people you killed.

176
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:30,564
How about the billion-peso fund
that I gave this family

177
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:32,733
while I was the mayor of this town?

178
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,528
Maybe, Papa, you should put that
in my accomplishments.

179
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:38,239
You should give credit to where it's due.

180
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:43,994
How will you handle a city's problems…

181
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:48,666
if you can't even handle your husband?

182
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:55,005
Fix your marriage,
and then come back to me.

183
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:57,925
[scoffs]

184
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:10,187
WE NEED TO TALK. IT'S IMPORTANT!

185
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:20,322
[tense music playing]

186
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:34,503
[heart monitor beeping rhythmically]

187
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,219
Do you know how long I've waited

188
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:25,012
for this opportunity?

189
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:32,978
If a person's heart is full of anger
and thoughts of revenge…

190
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:44,615
that person can do things they
never thought they could do.

191
00:14:01,632 --> 00:14:04,843
[suspenseful music]

192
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:16,230
[suspenseful music continues]

193
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:19,942
[heart monitor beeping rhythmically]

194
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:24,780
[door opens]

195
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:29,326
[door closes]

196
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:31,537
Nurse, has Emilia stopped by yet?

197
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:37,042
[suspenseful music continues]

198
00:14:39,169 --> 00:14:42,089
Nurse? Did the Ardientes stop by?

199
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:47,219
-[suspenseful music continues]
-[heart monitor beeping]

200
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:58,898
Anna!

201
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:03,193
Let go of me.

202
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:05,988
-Lily, let go of me.
-Shh… Keep it down.

203
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:08,073
What are you doing?
What are you planning to do?

204
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:10,200
Let me avenge Nanny Carlotta's death!

205
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:11,785
That monster needs to pay.

206
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:12,912
You don't need to do that.

207
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:15,789
-Ivy. Pick up the phone.
-[line ringing]

208
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:17,082
You need to stop Anna.

209
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:19,084
-Let me do this! Let go!
-I won't let you do this.

210
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,545
-Let go!
-Anna, I won't let you do this.

211
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,504
Put that thing down.

212
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:24,840
Let me do this, Ivy. Let go of me.

213
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:25,883
Let go--

214
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:27,384
I will kill this monster--

215
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,261
[Anna groans]

216
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:33,474
[tense music playing]

217
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:37,603
-[line ringing]
-Ivy!

218
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:40,940
This is going to get us in trouble!

219
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,738
You're actually going against me now?

220
00:15:47,821 --> 00:15:49,073
[cries]

221
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,243
-[sighs]
-[Anna crying]

222
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:56,664
I'm sorry.

223
00:15:56,747 --> 00:16:01,919
I'm sorry, Lily. Sorry! I'm so sorry!

224
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,754
-I'm sorry.
-[shushes]

225
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:08,133
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

226
00:16:08,509 --> 00:16:10,010
[shushes] Calm down.

227
00:16:14,598 --> 00:16:16,392
[Jepoy] What has gotten into you, Anna?!

228
00:16:16,475 --> 00:16:18,978
Why did you do that?
What were you thinking?!

229
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:24,566
Think about what would've
happened if they caught you.

230
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,068
You're a teacher, right?

231
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:28,487
What would've happened to you
if they had caught you?

232
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:32,825
Lily, I lost my old life

233
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:36,829
when I decided to come here
and assume your identity.

234
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:38,247
-Anna.
-Anna.

235
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:41,792
Do you think I can easily
go back to my old life

236
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:44,211
after I pretended to be Lily Cruz?!

237
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:47,214
How can I continue living
when all I can think about

238
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:49,425
is that the man
who murdered my foster mother

239
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:50,843
hasn't been punished yet?!

240
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:53,762
Why?! Did I ask you
to assume my identity?!

241
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:58,308
Did I beg you to?!
You both chose that, right?

242
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,644
You wanted that to happen, remember?

243
00:17:02,521 --> 00:17:05,733
Anna, I know you're affected.
And I respect that.

244
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:10,112
But I take responsibility
for everything that happened.

245
00:17:10,195 --> 00:17:13,699
I am doing everything to seek justice.

246
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:17,661
I plan everything carefully.
I think about my every move.

247
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:21,540
But what did you do?
You could've ruined all of it.

248
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:26,003
As a matter of fact, Anna,
I could easily hurt all of them.

249
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:28,839
I could easily kill them all,
but I refuse to do it

250
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:31,008
because I don't want to be like them.

251
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:35,137
Because I am not a murderer.
We are not murderers!

252
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:41,393
You want justice?
You want to seek justice?!

253
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:47,316
If you want justice,
then learn to cooperate.

254
00:17:47,399 --> 00:17:49,693
I'm telling you, Anna,
don't go against me!

255
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:52,696
Because the next time you do
something without telling me,

256
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,990
I don't know what I'll do to you!

257
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,658
Get your act together.

258
00:17:56,742 --> 00:17:58,160
[Diego] All right, calm down.

259
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:02,706
We're all here to fix the problem.

260
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,374
We're not here to fight.

261
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:07,961
We should try to be more understanding.

262
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:13,217
[Anna sobbing]

263
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:23,102
[Emilia] Papa is short-sighted.
He's an amnesiac.

264
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:26,563
<i>Why do I have to patch things</i>
<i>up with Raul just to get back</i>

265
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,065
into power, Jaguar?

266
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:29,483
You know, I don't get it.

267
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:31,401
[sighs]

268
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:33,987
Can you just help me plan a plot?

269
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:35,864
A coup against my Papa?

270
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:40,244
Why don't you give your husband
another chance?

271
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:42,830
[sighs] Because I don't love Raul anymore.

272
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:47,167
<i>I can only think of you.</i>

273
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,461
I can see us together, Jaguar.

274
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,213
[exhales]

275
00:18:52,005 --> 00:18:53,465
I'm sorry, Emilia.

276
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:58,762
Hello? Jaguar?

277
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:09,314
Why did you have to be so stubborn?

278
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,941
Haven't you learned from my mistakes?

279
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:12,901
[Anna sobs]

280
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,989
I know I said some harsh words to Anna.

281
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:20,325
But I'm only thinking
about your well-being.

282
00:19:21,034 --> 00:19:21,910
[Jepoy] Anna.

283
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:26,665
I didn't mean to shout at you earlier.

284
00:19:26,748 --> 00:19:29,334
No, Jepoy. It's my fault. [sniffles]

285
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:32,337
I should've listened to Lily and to you.

286
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:37,009
Ivy, Anna looks up to you.
I'm sure she understands.

287
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:41,763
Besides, you're best friends.
Everything will be all right.

288
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:47,102
I'm sorry, Jepoy. I hope you forgive me.

289
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,479
I hope Lily can still forgive me.

290
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:53,483
Hush now. Stop crying.

291
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:01,116
-Mom, I have to go.
-Take care, dear.

292
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,701
-Diego.
-Take care, Ivy.

293
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,203
Please take care of them.

294
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,454
I will.

295
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:08,040
[soft music playing]

296
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:16,673
Lily.

297
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:21,136
[soft music continues]

298
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:22,804
I'm sorry.

299
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:28,101
Sorry!

300
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:32,856
[soft music continues]

301
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,953
Poor little Raul.

302
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:48,330
Who would've thought
that you'd be involved

303
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:50,958
in a love triangle between you,

304
00:20:51,541 --> 00:20:56,338
Emilia, and another version of yourself?

305
00:20:56,922 --> 00:21:00,300
Isn't that crazy? It's so twisted!

306
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:03,387
And, it's so exciting.

307
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,014
But you know what?

308
00:21:06,848 --> 00:21:11,395
What's more exciting
is your annulment with Emilia.

309
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:18,151
There won't be an annulment.

310
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,282
What are you saying?

311
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:27,953
That you'll choose Emilia over me?

312
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:32,666
Wait. Choose? Why do I have to choose now?

313
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:34,710
Aren't we just helping each other?

314
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:36,795
We're just using each other.

315
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,257
-Yes.
-So?

316
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:42,676
But, I'm selfish.

317
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:46,221
What's mine is mine.

318
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:49,933
You. You're all mine.

319
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:52,853
Even if we're just using each other.

320
00:21:52,936 --> 00:21:55,647
[tense music playing]

321
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:08,869
[club music playing]

322
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:12,622
Emilia. You're here. Good evening.

323
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,208
There's nothing good about it.

324
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,711
Are you really not going
to leave me alone?

325
00:22:17,794 --> 00:22:19,713
Do you really want to go against me?

326
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:24,843
I know we fight about a lot of things.

327
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:29,097
And we've even tried to have
each other killed lots of times.

328
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:32,017
But, in the end, we get along.

329
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:39,316
Yes. Do you know why?
It's hard to eliminate you.

330
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:42,486
Until now, you're still here.
I can't get rid of you.

331
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:49,117
Admit it, Emilia.
I could be of some use to you.

332
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:53,413
I have information.

333
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:57,584
And I know, you'll be interested.

334
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:01,338
Lunch tomorrow?

335
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:05,050
[tense music playing]

336
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:15,018
You should've seen your mom's face.

337
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,103
[scoffs]

338
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:19,147
She was blaming Ivy

339
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:22,818
for convincing me
to hold that press conference.

340
00:23:24,319 --> 00:23:26,863
Silly little girls!

341
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:30,909
They both think they can outwit
and manipulate me.

342
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,327
[scoffs]

343
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:39,876
[suspenseful music playing]

344
00:23:42,295 --> 00:23:44,631
You're really testing my patience, Ivy.

345
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:47,592
Excuse me?

346
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:50,637
Don't act as if I don't know.

347
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:54,015
It's pretty obvious. [chuckles]

348
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:56,935
Lately, I noticed that Papa
has been taking your side.

349
00:23:57,018 --> 00:24:00,188
First, Arnaldo's psych counseling.

350
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:04,734
Second, the press conference.
What are you trying to prove?

351
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:07,028
That you're the apple of Papa's eye?!

352
00:24:07,612 --> 00:24:09,114
But you still came here.

353
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:13,034
Don't get jealous, Emilia. It's all right.

354
00:24:14,286 --> 00:24:17,747
Emilia, we don't have to be friends.

355
00:24:18,665 --> 00:24:21,209
But we do have to get along

356
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:24,504
if we want to protect
each other's interests.

357
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:29,134
Actually, I'm the one
who should be mad at you.

358
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:33,180
You wanted to have me killed
on my wedding day, remember?

359
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:37,851
But, here I am,
trying to let go of that issue

360
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:41,813
because Arnaldo is more important to me.

361
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:47,527
I don't believe you've forgiven
Arnaldo for killing

362
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,654
that mother figure of yours.

363
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:53,283
And I especially
don't believe you love him.

364
00:24:53,366 --> 00:24:57,704
I won't waste my time
trying to convince you.

365
00:24:57,787 --> 00:24:59,664
What do you know about love, Ivy?

366
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:04,628
What about you?
You have no moral ascendancy.

367
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:07,172
You're getting an annulment, right?

368
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:11,551
How dare you?!

369
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:13,929
Careful.

370
00:25:14,971 --> 00:25:19,976
If I were you, I would stop
playing hard to get,

371
00:25:20,477 --> 00:25:23,980
because Raul might grow tired
of chasing after you,

372
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:25,440
and he might start pursuing other women.

373
00:25:25,523 --> 00:25:28,860
-I don't care!
-Really?

374
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:32,239
[tense music playing]

375
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:39,496
Natalie and Raul are together in a hotel.

376
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,457
Hmm… What could they
possibly be doing there?

377
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:49,547
[tense music playing]

378
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:58,390
Your husband is fooling you again.

379
00:25:59,849 --> 00:26:04,980
But, that's okay. You're getting
an annulment anyway, right?

380
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:11,194
What pleasure do you get
from seeing me getting hurt?

381
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:12,862
Are you still affected by it?

382
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:16,700
I thought it didn't mean anything
to you anymore. Sorry.

383
00:26:17,325 --> 00:26:19,953
But that really is
what I wanted to show you.

384
00:26:23,581 --> 00:26:27,419
I will tear that woman into pieces.

385
00:26:28,503 --> 00:26:30,380
That, I'll surely do.

386
00:26:30,463 --> 00:26:33,675
[tense music playing]

387
00:26:42,976 --> 00:26:44,436
Colonel, any updates?

388
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:46,980
Congressman, I've already dealt
with the reporters

389
00:26:47,063 --> 00:26:48,648
trying to ruin the mayor's reputation.

390
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:51,026
They kept asking when he'll recover.

391
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:56,406
He'll wake up soon.
My grandson has an iron will…

392
00:26:57,198 --> 00:27:00,660
a campaign to run, and an election to win.

393
00:27:01,202 --> 00:27:03,288
What do you plan to do with Diego Torillo?

394
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:06,791
He's starting up a ruckus again.
Just say the word.

395
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:08,209
My men are ready.

396
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:10,712
Not so fast, Colonel.

397
00:27:11,504 --> 00:27:14,007
Contrary to what people believe,

398
00:27:14,090 --> 00:27:16,301
I do have a sense of diplomacy.

399
00:27:18,094 --> 00:27:23,099
Send a message to Diego Torillo.
We need to talk.

400
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:24,267
Yes, sir.

401
00:27:27,479 --> 00:27:29,064
-Will that be okay?
-Yes, sir.

402
00:27:30,148 --> 00:27:31,858
Hold on, are we expecting someone?

403
00:27:32,942 --> 00:27:33,985
[man] No.

404
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:41,326
-Soldiers?
-Be alert.

405
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:43,495
[tense music playing]

406
00:27:47,707 --> 00:27:48,792
Wait.

407
00:27:51,169 --> 00:27:53,880
You're armed. What are you doing here?

408
00:27:54,172 --> 00:27:56,841
I'm not here to cause trouble.
I have a message

409
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:59,511
from Congressman Ardiente
for Diego Torillo.

410
00:28:02,764 --> 00:28:03,765
-Oh.
-Call them.

411
00:28:03,848 --> 00:28:04,933
Yes, Jepoy.

412
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:15,860
[tense music playing]

413
00:28:21,408 --> 00:28:22,534
[Loring] What's this?

414
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:26,121
[Diego] Nanny.

415
00:28:28,957 --> 00:28:32,168
I'm Diego Torillo. Why are you here?

416
00:28:32,961 --> 00:28:35,422
Congressman Ardiente asked me
to give you this.

417
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:38,967
[tense music playing]

418
00:28:56,484 --> 00:28:58,820
WE HAVE LOTS TO DISCUSS.
LET'S MEET AT THE PLAZA LATER.

419
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:01,030
PLEASE GRANT MY REQUEST.
CONGRESSMAN JULIO ARDIENTE

420
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:06,870
The congressman wants to meet with me.

421
00:29:06,953 --> 00:29:10,123
[Loring] Don't even think
of granting that request.

422
00:29:10,206 --> 00:29:12,876
-That might be a trap.
-They're right, Diego.

423
00:29:12,959 --> 00:29:14,711
I won't fall for their trap.

424
00:29:15,503 --> 00:29:19,924
If the congressman wants
to talk, then I won't back down.

425
00:29:20,008 --> 00:29:21,634
Diego, I'll come with you.

426
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:24,012
[Marlon] Batch.

427
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:29,517
[Raul] Let's just do that. Let's meet up.

428
00:29:30,643 --> 00:29:32,312
Okay, I'll call you later. Thank you.

429
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:49,913
[tense music playing]

430
00:29:49,996 --> 00:29:52,165
[phone ringing]

431
00:29:57,295 --> 00:30:00,215
I HAVE A SURPRISE FOR YOU.
LET'S MEET. SAME TIME AND PLACE.

432
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,312
Prove to me that you're on my side.

433
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:18,149
Join me in this war I'm going into.

434
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:21,486
I don't have to prove anything, Emilia.

435
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:27,742
But I'll go with you just for fun.

436
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:31,871
Great. Let's go.

437
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:44,676
I'm here.

438
00:30:46,219 --> 00:30:48,805
Raul? Ooh.

439
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:52,350
You really set it up nicely, huh?

440
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:55,144
Raul?

441
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:59,440
Did you miss me?

442
00:31:02,277 --> 00:31:04,028
Surprise!

443
00:31:04,737 --> 00:31:08,449
[laughs] Why am I not surprised?

444
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:11,661
-Do you want a surprise?
-[Natalie grunts]

445
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:19,127
You snot-nosed bitch.

446
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:24,299
[chuckles]

447
00:31:25,174 --> 00:31:28,553
[foreboding music playing]

448
00:31:43,943 --> 00:31:45,528
-This way.
-A reporter.

449
00:31:45,612 --> 00:31:49,198
Congressman Julio! We'd like
to ask a few questions!

450
00:31:49,282 --> 00:31:50,992
Are you here to see Diego Torillo?

451
00:31:51,075 --> 00:31:52,994
-Congressman!
-Here for Diego Torillo?

452
00:31:53,077 --> 00:31:54,913
-Congressman Julio…
-Any statement?

453
00:31:54,996 --> 00:31:56,289
Congressman!

454
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:07,175
[reporter] Mr. Diego, thoughts
on the congressman's visit?

455
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:13,014
Boys.

456
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:17,101
Diego, Diego, Diego…

457
00:32:18,394 --> 00:32:21,314
You didn't need to bring
the whole village.

458
00:32:23,107 --> 00:32:25,026
You even brought Lily Cruz too.

459
00:32:25,902 --> 00:32:27,153
Oh! And Madrigal!

460
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:30,490
You look a lot better
than the last time I saw you.

461
00:32:32,325 --> 00:32:33,576
What do you need?

462
00:32:34,285 --> 00:32:37,914
Diego, for now, I'd like you to refrain

463
00:32:37,997 --> 00:32:40,917
from refiling charges against Arnaldo.

464
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:41,960
[scoffs]

465
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:44,963
I'm afraid I can't give you
what you're asking for.

466
00:32:45,046 --> 00:32:46,422
[tut-tuts]

467
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:49,759
You know, we're starting
on the wrong foot again.

468
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:51,427
You don't understand.

469
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:55,932
What I'm telling you
is not a request. It's an order.

470
00:32:56,015 --> 00:32:58,977
[tense music playing]

471
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:17,453
[Natalie] Emilia and Ivy?

472
00:33:18,287 --> 00:33:21,416
No way! [laughs]

473
00:33:21,499 --> 00:33:24,752
This is fun! I'm impressed!

474
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:32,218
So, this kinda seems familiar. Right?

475
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:33,928
Yes, Natalie.

476
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:37,724
The three little witches meet again.

477
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:41,436
-[Natalie scoffs]
-But this time, you're the one tied up.

478
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,022
What was that again?

479
00:33:44,605 --> 00:33:46,983
You know, I have trouble remembering.

480
00:33:47,066 --> 00:33:48,401
Was that…

481
00:33:50,820 --> 00:33:52,989
[laughs]

482
00:33:53,448 --> 00:33:55,033
No, it doesn't suit me.

483
00:33:56,075 --> 00:33:57,618
Could you hold this for me, Ivy?

484
00:33:58,953 --> 00:34:00,538
Was that, um…

485
00:34:00,872 --> 00:34:02,749
-[Emilia] One slap? Two slaps?
-[Natalie grunts]

486
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:06,544
And the third one will be for
you sleeping with my husband!

487
00:34:10,131 --> 00:34:12,759
[laughs]

488
00:34:13,509 --> 00:34:16,971
I missed you too, Emilia. But guess what?

489
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:20,975
The fact of the matter is, I'm back.

490
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:24,520
And I slept with him,

491
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:27,190
and am sleeping,

492
00:34:27,273 --> 00:34:32,987
and <i>will be</i> sleeping with him
until I forget how to bend over!

493
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:34,072
[Emilia grunts]

494
00:34:36,365 --> 00:34:38,951
-Emilia. Emilia, calm down.
-Do it.

495
00:34:39,494 --> 00:34:43,623
-Emilia, no.
-Calm down?! Calm down?!

496
00:34:43,706 --> 00:34:47,251
I am so sick and tired of people
telling me to calm down!

497
00:34:47,335 --> 00:34:49,253
-I am so tired!
-[gunshot]

498
00:34:49,337 --> 00:34:50,755
-I've had enough!
-[gunshots]

499
00:34:50,838 --> 00:34:51,672
Emilia!

500
00:34:51,756 --> 00:34:54,217
[screams] I don't want to calm down now!

501
00:35:00,473 --> 00:35:03,059
You think Ivy Aguas is on your side.

502
00:35:03,726 --> 00:35:09,482
But you know that from the start,
she has been your worst enemy!

503
00:35:09,982 --> 00:35:14,278
She successfully snaked your son Arnaldo

504
00:35:14,362 --> 00:35:17,073
and made him fall in love.
And now, she left him for dead!

505
00:35:17,156 --> 00:35:18,699
And guess who she's coming after?

506
00:35:21,285 --> 00:35:22,161
You!

507
00:35:22,245 --> 00:35:24,539
[tense music playing]

508
00:35:31,587 --> 00:35:32,630
Try it.

509
00:35:35,007 --> 00:35:37,802
See if you can pull the trigger
before I bash your face.

510
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,305
[Emilia screaming]

511
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:44,225
-Enough! Enough!
-[gunshot]

512
00:35:44,684 --> 00:35:45,643
[Emilia screaming]

513
00:35:45,726 --> 00:35:47,436
-Stop it!
-You're crazy!

514
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:49,480
-So what if I'm crazy?!
-Emilia!

515
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:51,524
So what if I'm crazy?!

516
00:35:51,607 --> 00:35:56,362
Don't kill that woman.
I'm just here for fun, remember?

517
00:35:56,904 --> 00:36:00,283
If you kill her, I won't
help you clean up her body.

518
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:13,421
Be thankful I'm not one
for cleaning messes.

519
00:36:13,504 --> 00:36:16,716
If I was, I'd end you now.

520
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:19,385
But I'm warning you.

521
00:36:19,468 --> 00:36:24,015
If you sleep with my husband
again, I will kill you.

522
00:36:24,098 --> 00:36:26,475
I will definitely kill you!

523
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:32,440
Oops. [chuckles]

524
00:36:32,523 --> 00:36:37,028
I forgot something. I need a souvenir.

525
00:36:37,778 --> 00:36:39,697
Give me your best smile.

526
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:40,823
[Emilia] Ugh.

527
00:36:41,616 --> 00:36:43,743
[laughs]

528
00:36:43,826 --> 00:36:46,829
You're crazy! Nutjob!

529
00:36:46,913 --> 00:36:51,209
That's right! Since the start! [laughs]

530
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:53,127
[Emilia laughing]

531
00:36:53,794 --> 00:36:57,798
Congratulations, Natalie.
You're still alive.

532
00:36:58,841 --> 00:37:01,219
Thank me next time.

533
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:05,681
[dramatic music]

534
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:08,392
Where are you going?

535
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:10,645
Bye.

536
00:37:12,897 --> 00:37:14,941
Ivy? Hey!

537
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:18,736
Don't leave me here, you two witches!

538
00:37:19,403 --> 00:37:20,696
You're both nuts!

539
00:37:25,868 --> 00:37:27,078
Do you actually think

540
00:37:27,161 --> 00:37:31,123
I'll let you kick Arnaldo while he's down?

541
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:34,168
You're blind to your own arrogance.

542
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:37,505
You think everyone who isn't
an Ardiente is dumb.

543
00:37:38,089 --> 00:37:39,423
But the truth is,

544
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:41,926
you're the only ones
who still believe you're smart.

545
00:37:43,844 --> 00:37:45,680
This town is spitting you out.

546
00:37:46,555 --> 00:37:50,393
My, strong words. Can you back them up?

547
00:37:51,727 --> 00:37:55,606
I'm running for governor
so that the common people

548
00:37:55,690 --> 00:37:58,693
have a voice against people like you.

549
00:37:59,694 --> 00:38:03,489
That's why Arnaldo will pay
for all his crimes,

550
00:38:03,572 --> 00:38:04,532
whether he likes it or not.

551
00:38:05,616 --> 00:38:06,993
Okay, suit yourself

552
00:38:07,076 --> 00:38:13,374
if you want to play the small-town hero
that you've always aspired to be.

553
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:16,294
But don't tell me
I didn't warn you, Diego.

554
00:38:16,919 --> 00:38:18,587
You're going up against a behemoth.

555
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:21,132
You're going up against me.

556
00:38:21,757 --> 00:38:24,969
And after the battle,
when the smoke has cleared,

557
00:38:25,636 --> 00:38:28,180
your death will be very biblical.

558
00:38:28,514 --> 00:38:31,183
To paraphrase a line in the Old Testament,

559
00:38:31,726 --> 00:38:35,855
"I will reduce you to ashes and dust."

560
00:38:39,191 --> 00:38:42,778
Miss Lily Cruz.
Finally, I get to meet you.

561
00:38:43,070 --> 00:38:45,281
Television doesn't do you justice.

562
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:48,951
You look better in person. [chuckles]

563
00:38:50,411 --> 00:38:51,454
Oh, well.

564
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:54,415
[tense music playing]

565
00:38:57,209 --> 00:39:00,755
Excuse me. My, my.

566
00:39:01,088 --> 00:39:04,550
Madrigal, what a big gun you have.

567
00:39:05,801 --> 00:39:06,969
Ooh!

568
00:39:07,303 --> 00:39:08,346
Jepoy.

569
00:39:13,225 --> 00:39:14,352
Please?

570
00:39:17,063 --> 00:39:18,105
Jepoy.

571
00:39:24,820 --> 00:39:25,821
[scoffs]

572
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:29,992
Amateurs. I'm going up against amateurs.

573
00:39:30,076 --> 00:39:32,036
[reporter] Congressman Julio! Sir!

574
00:39:32,119 --> 00:39:34,288
[indistinct chatter]

575
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:35,706
[reporter] Mr. Diego, what did you

576
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,124
and Congressman Julio talk about?

577
00:39:47,843 --> 00:39:49,637
[Camia] Is it true that the Ardientes

578
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:52,640
stole this farmland from your forefathers?

579
00:39:52,723 --> 00:39:54,225
Yes, Miss Camia.

580
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:57,436
Ivy Aguas was supposed
to set up a business here.

581
00:39:57,520 --> 00:40:01,649
But she backed out because
of the rights of the farmers.

582
00:40:01,732 --> 00:40:03,984
Do you know any other scandals

583
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:06,237
or corrupt activities of the Ardientes?

584
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:11,242
It's scary to speak out.
Their loyalists might find out.

585
00:40:11,742 --> 00:40:13,619
But somebody over there can help.

586
00:40:13,702 --> 00:40:16,705
As far as I know, she used to be
an employee at city hall,

587
00:40:16,789 --> 00:40:18,165
when Emilia Ardiente was still the mayor.

588
00:40:18,249 --> 00:40:21,127
-Where does she live?
-Right down the road.

589
00:40:22,586 --> 00:40:25,714
-Okay, thank you.
-Okay. Let's go.

590
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:30,136
I told you, Emilia.

591
00:40:30,219 --> 00:40:34,181
We don't need to be friends
just to have fun.

592
00:40:35,975 --> 00:40:40,062
So, Ivy, why don't you sponsor
my candidacy?

593
00:40:40,146 --> 00:40:42,440
Maybe someday, we could be running mates.

594
00:40:42,773 --> 00:40:44,066
Isn't that exciting?

595
00:40:44,900 --> 00:40:46,944
You're trying to sell me something again?

596
00:40:47,027 --> 00:40:51,449
Tell me, Emilia.
Why should I enter politics?

597
00:40:51,532 --> 00:40:54,326
Because in politics, it's like a jungle.

598
00:40:54,743 --> 00:40:57,288
Just hesitate,
and you'll get bitten by snakes.

599
00:40:57,371 --> 00:41:00,749
I don't need to enter politics
to know that.

600
00:41:00,833 --> 00:41:02,376
Okay, okay, okay.

601
00:41:03,210 --> 00:41:06,839
Politics is something
beyond what you can imagine.

602
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,549
You can get anything that you like.

603
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:11,385
It has its own perks, Ivy.

604
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:13,637
And you can actually steal billions.

605
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:16,182
[laughs] Oh, shoot.

606
00:41:16,265 --> 00:41:17,266
Billions?

607
00:41:17,349 --> 00:41:19,435
That's supposed to be a secret, okay?

608
00:41:21,103 --> 00:41:26,775
Lips are sealed. Cheers. Lips are sealed!

609
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:28,944
[laughing]

610
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:33,449
-[Diego] Nanny, Uncle.
-[Loring] Thank goodness…

611
00:41:33,532 --> 00:41:35,534
-Diego.
-you're back safe…

612
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:38,370
-and sound. Oh, my.
-Yes, son.

613
00:41:38,454 --> 00:41:43,209
That old man's this close
to meeting his maker,

614
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:45,127
-and he still hasn't changed!
-[Pandoy laughs]

615
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:47,713
But you know, Miss Loring,
Diego was pretty cool earlier.

616
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:50,758
He faced Julio Ardiente head on!

617
00:41:50,841 --> 00:41:53,010
Yeah, he never backs down
from a challenge.

618
00:41:53,093 --> 00:41:56,931
[laughs] Still, you should
be careful, son.

619
00:41:57,014 --> 00:41:59,600
Julio's a cunning man!

620
00:41:59,683 --> 00:42:02,895
-Of course, Uncle. Don't worry.
-Yes.

621
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:05,481
By the way, where's Auntie Camia?

622
00:42:05,564 --> 00:42:08,359
Oh, she had some errand
at the cooperative.

623
00:42:19,036 --> 00:42:21,497
-Um… Excuse me.
-Yes?

624
00:42:21,580 --> 00:42:23,499
Do you know where Miss Cora lives?

625
00:42:23,582 --> 00:42:26,919
Oh, yes. Over there. The lady sweeping.

626
00:42:27,002 --> 00:42:29,004
-Oh, thank you.
-No problem.

627
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:41,642
Excuse me, is this where Miss Cora lives?

628
00:42:41,725 --> 00:42:44,853
Oh, that's me. And, you are?

629
00:42:44,937 --> 00:42:46,313
I'm Camia Cruz.

630
00:42:46,397 --> 00:42:47,731
Oh, aren't you the one

631
00:42:47,815 --> 00:42:51,443
supporting Diego Torillo for governor?

632
00:42:52,403 --> 00:42:55,990
Yes. I was hoping to ask you
some questions if that's okay.

633
00:42:56,073 --> 00:42:57,408
About what?

634
00:42:58,617 --> 00:43:00,244
About the Ardientes.

635
00:43:00,911 --> 00:43:06,083
I heard you served as Emilia's secretary

636
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:07,543
when she was still mayor.

637
00:43:08,294 --> 00:43:11,255
Oh, my, that was such a long time ago.

638
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:15,259
Actually, I was hoping you could help me.

639
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:17,678
I'm sorry.

640
00:43:17,761 --> 00:43:19,346
But, I still have lots of chores to do.

641
00:43:37,197 --> 00:43:39,199
[no audio]

642
00:43:51,295 --> 00:43:53,797
You liar! Cheater!

643
00:43:54,506 --> 00:43:56,383
You're still sleeping with Natalie.

644
00:43:57,718 --> 00:44:00,554
Hold on. What? Emilia, where'd you hear?

645
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:01,639
-No!
-Wait.

646
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:05,017
Here! So, stop lying to me!

647
00:44:05,476 --> 00:44:07,478
I saw everything! I caught you red-handed!

648
00:44:08,270 --> 00:44:09,396
Raul…

649
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:12,566
You don't want to file for annulment,

650
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:14,318
you don't want to sign the papers,

651
00:44:14,401 --> 00:44:16,028
and yet, you're still cheating on me!

652
00:44:16,111 --> 00:44:17,529
-Wait, wait, wait!
-No, I've had it!

653
00:44:17,613 --> 00:44:19,114
-Emilia, wait!
-Enough is enough!

654
00:44:19,198 --> 00:44:20,824
-I've had enough.
-Wait.

655
00:44:20,908 --> 00:44:25,120
-Let me explain! Emilia, please. Emilia!
-No! No.

656
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,955
-No.
-Not like this, Emilia…

657
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:28,040
-No!
-Let's talk this through.

658
00:44:28,123 --> 00:44:29,500
-Enough talk, Raul!
-Please.

659
00:44:29,583 --> 00:44:30,876
-We're over, Raul!
-Please, stop.

660
00:44:30,959 --> 00:44:35,005
No! You, get out of my house!

661
00:44:35,089 --> 00:44:38,509
And you get out of my life!
We're over, Raul.

662
00:44:38,592 --> 00:44:40,678
-Emilia.
-I've had enough!

663
00:44:40,761 --> 00:44:42,096
-I'm sorry.
-I've had it.

664
00:44:42,179 --> 00:44:43,472
Emilia… Emilia!

665
00:44:55,150 --> 00:44:58,070
[heart monitor beeping]

666
00:45:02,074 --> 00:45:03,200
[Emilia] Arnaldo?

667
00:45:05,786 --> 00:45:10,958
[exhales] Son! You're awake! You're awake!

668
00:45:14,420 --> 00:45:16,004
He's awake now.

669
00:45:17,756 --> 00:45:19,133
Papa, he's awake!

670
00:45:24,555 --> 00:45:27,975
[tense music playing]

671
00:45:54,168 --> 00:45:58,005
Miss Cora, I'm begging you.
Please help us.

672
00:45:58,088 --> 00:46:00,883
We could really use your statement.

673
00:46:00,966 --> 00:46:03,177
It would be a big help to us.

674
00:46:04,595 --> 00:46:07,806
Aren't you afraid I might tell
the Ardientes what you're doing?

675
00:46:08,724 --> 00:46:11,226
Miss Cora, I'm just taking a chance.

676
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,603
Even just a lead.

677
00:46:12,686 --> 00:46:16,356
Maybe you can give us something,
so we'll know where to start.

678
00:46:18,442 --> 00:46:21,778
Are you sure you don't work
for the Ardientes?

679
00:46:26,074 --> 00:46:27,117
[sighs]

680
00:46:27,201 --> 00:46:29,745
We're victims
of the Ardientes too, Miss Cora.

681
00:46:29,828 --> 00:46:34,625
I'm doing this so that, one day,
the citizens of this town

682
00:46:34,708 --> 00:46:37,252
can break free
from the Ardientes' tyranny.

683
00:46:37,836 --> 00:46:40,172
So, I hope you'll help us.

684
00:46:42,716 --> 00:46:44,551
[doctor] The mayor needs to
undergo consultation

685
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:46,303
psychiatric before we discharge him.

686
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:50,474
And we need to do this, or else,
his condition could worsen.

687
00:46:50,557 --> 00:46:54,186
How long will this all take, doc?

688
00:46:54,269 --> 00:46:56,438
The results of the assessment

689
00:46:56,522 --> 00:46:58,732
will depend on his reaction to the tests.

690
00:46:58,815 --> 00:47:02,819
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah,
blah, blah. Look at him go.

691
00:47:02,903 --> 00:47:06,573
Doc, my grandson is well. Can't you see?

692
00:47:06,657 --> 00:47:10,619
His brain is as tough as anything can get.

693
00:47:10,702 --> 00:47:13,622
Now, please, could you please

694
00:47:13,705 --> 00:47:17,543
just release him from this dreary place?

695
00:47:17,626 --> 00:47:18,710
But, Congressman--

696
00:47:18,794 --> 00:47:23,715
Doc, your parents sent you
to medical school for 10 years.

697
00:47:23,799 --> 00:47:29,888
After 10 years, you had
an internship and whatnot.

698
00:47:29,972 --> 00:47:33,141
And diagnosis, prognosis, and… [inhales]

699
00:47:33,225 --> 00:47:36,395
…whatever nose-in, nose-out
you talk about.

700
00:47:36,478 --> 00:47:39,565
Anyway, don't put your studies to waste.

701
00:47:39,648 --> 00:47:41,483
Because if I lose my patience,

702
00:47:41,567 --> 00:47:43,777
I might just have your license pulled.

703
00:47:45,362 --> 00:47:46,405
[Julio sighs]

704
00:47:55,163 --> 00:47:58,458
-[muffled scream]
-[Arnaldo grunting]

705
00:48:00,669 --> 00:48:04,047
-[Arnaldo] <i>What about her?</i>
<i>-You shouldn't trust her.</i>

706
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,632
[Arnaldo] <i>That's not true.</i>
<i>That's not true.</i>

707
00:48:05,716 --> 00:48:08,552
[Nimfa] <i>She's the one feeding</i>
<i>information to Diego's camp.</i>

708
00:48:08,635 --> 00:48:09,678
That's not true.

709
00:48:09,761 --> 00:48:12,431
[Nimfa] <i>She's Diego's spy</i>
<i>within the Ardiente family!</i>

710
00:48:12,514 --> 00:48:14,266
<i>She's just using you.</i>

711
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:16,101
[Nimfa] <i>Mayor, you need to know</i>
<i>that Ivy is--</i>

712
00:48:16,184 --> 00:48:18,186
-<i>That's not true!</i>
-[gunshots]

713
00:48:18,270 --> 00:48:20,439
-[gunshots]
-[Arnaldo screaming]

714
00:48:22,232 --> 00:48:23,942
[gasps]

715
00:48:26,445 --> 00:48:28,030
[door opening]

716
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:45,005
Ivy. Just… Just stay there.

717
00:48:46,757 --> 00:48:47,841
Stay there.

718
00:48:52,220 --> 00:48:55,474
-Don't come near me. Don't.
-Mayor?

719
00:48:55,557 --> 00:48:57,017
Don't come any closer! Stay there!

720
00:48:57,100 --> 00:48:58,393
-Stay there!
-Mayor, what's wrong?

721
00:48:58,477 --> 00:48:59,770
-Don't touch me!
-Mayor.

722
00:48:59,853 --> 00:49:00,896
Don't touch me!

723
00:49:00,979 --> 00:49:02,314
-Help is coming--
-Don't touch me!

724
00:49:02,397 --> 00:49:04,524
-Don't touch me!
-Doc, nurse, help!

725
00:49:04,608 --> 00:49:05,984
-Don't touch me!
-Mayor, no!

726
00:49:06,068 --> 00:49:10,989
-Don't touch me! [grunts]
-Mayor! Mayor! Mayor, no!

727
00:49:11,073 --> 00:49:12,866
-[nurse grunts]
-Don't touch me!

728
00:49:14,159 --> 00:49:16,411
Don't… Don't touch me!

729
00:49:17,621 --> 00:49:18,830
[groaning]

730
00:49:21,041 --> 00:49:22,918
[tense music playing]

731
00:49:25,629 --> 00:49:26,880
<i>Where are you taking me?</i>

732
00:49:26,963 --> 00:49:28,131
[doctor] <i>The mayor is dangerous.</i>

733
00:49:28,215 --> 00:49:30,467
<i>That's why we moved him</i>
<i>to the psychiatric ward.</i>

734
00:49:30,550 --> 00:49:32,010
[Julio] <i>You'll get better. But not here.</i>

735
00:49:32,094 --> 00:49:34,763
<i>You will spend time in our rest house.</i>

736
00:49:35,097 --> 00:49:36,932
[Arnaldo] <i>I want Ivy to come with me.</i>

737
00:49:37,015 --> 00:49:39,768
[Diego] <i>Arnaldo isn't thinking straight.</i>
<i>Get out of there.</i>

738
00:49:41,311 --> 00:49:46,942
<i>I'm going to finish this.</i>
<i>You shouldn't trust Ivy Aguas.</i>

739
00:49:47,025 --> 00:49:51,822
<i>She's been lying to you.</i>
